Subject: virtio/fs: let the caller own files in access checks

A guest mounting a LinuxSimplifiedFixedOwner share with an option that
shows every file as owned by the caller turns off local permission checks
and sends access(2) to the host, which compared the caller against the
fixed owner. A non-root caller then got only the "other" bits of a file
it appears to own: PHP is_writable() on a 0755 directory returned false
while writes succeeded. set_caller_owns(true) checks the owner bits for
every caller instead.

